    {
      "id": "3967620445197216169",
      "external_id": "3967620445197216169",
      "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DcP0cYHjqmp/",
      "author": "b.withrwc",
      "author_name": "brooke humphrey",
      "author_id": "47290051",
      "published_at": "2026-08-20T03:40:36.000Z",
      "text": "Tomorrow doesn\u2019t start at 5am, it starts at 8pm \ud83e\udef6\ud83c\udffd\n\nHere\u2019s what I\u2019ve learned after years of \u201ctrying\u201d to be a morning person: motivation is not the variable. Friction is.\n\nThe morning you skip isn\u2019t usually the one you didn\u2019t want bad enough, it\u2019s the one where you had to find your shoes, decide what to eat, refill your water, and figure out what you were even doing that day, all before your brain came online. That\u2019s four decisions standing between you and the thing you said mattered. Tired-you loses that fight almost every time.\n\nSo I stopped trying to be more disciplined at 5am and started being more prepared at 8pm.\n\nNone of these take more than a few minutes (at most) and all of them make the next morning feel like it\u2019s on my side. That\u2019s really what prep is, it\u2019s not productivity, it\u2019s kindness. It\u2019s you deciding ahead of time to make things easier for the version of you who\u2019s going to be tired, cold, and short on willpower.\n\nAnd I\u2019d rather build a life where I don\u2019t have to white-knuckle every good decision. Where obedience and consistency feel less like a fight and more like a path that\u2019s already been cleared.\n\nStart with one. Pick the thing that makes your mornings hardest and remove it the night before. Do that for a week and tell me what changes. \ud83e\udef6\ud83c\udffd\n\nWhich one are you stealing tonight? \ud83d\udc47\ud83c\udffd\n\n#fitness #inspiration #habits #dothework",
      "media_type": "Sidecar",
      "hashtags": [
        "fitness",
        "inspiration",
        "habits",
        "dothework"
      ],
      "raw_metrics": {
        "like_count": 1,
        "comments_count": 1
      }
    },
